## Implementation discipline (docs/ENGINEERING.md)
- Before substantial edits, state consequential assumptions and pair each step with an observable check. Ask only when ambiguity materially changes scope, contracts, authorization or irreversible outcomes; otherwise use documented, reversible judgment.
- Prefer the smallest complete solution that satisfies the accepted requirements; new layers, packages, dependencies and configuration need a present use case. Simplicity never removes required authentication, validation, concurrency and recovery behavior.
- Keep the diff tied to the selected task; match local style; remove code made unused by the change after checking its consumers; record unrelated findings separately.
- Reproduce behavioral defects before fixing them when feasible; verify the actual assertion the acceptance criterion makes; report checks not run honestly.
- Scale ceremony to risk: a documentation edit needs focused inspection, not extra verification rounds.

## Efficiency
- Search narrowly before reading full files; exclude generated/vendor/build folders. Do not read all task bodies; read the index, the selected task and its linked context.
- No verbose logs or repeated full reports in handoffs; link evidence files. Save state at task boundaries so a fresh session resumes from docs/HANDOFF.md.
- For visible UI progress follow docs/VISUAL-PROGRESS.md; relay real screenshot files with captions or clickable paths, never a claimed capture without the file.

## Design resources
For UI work read docs/DESIGN-WORKFLOW.md, design/BRAND.md and the relevant design/briefs/<surface>.md; design/catalog.json only when it lists assets. While BRAND.md is unresolved and the catalog is empty, branding is pending: unknown values stay proposed, never invented. Canonical sources stay in design/; applications consume versioned runtime exports.

## Product language
End-user texts are in `{{PRODUCT_LANGUAGE}}`; all project documentation, task files, evidence and communication with the owner are in English unless the owner says otherwise.

